1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:04,600
Nine days ago, Maria asked a dealership
about a blue RAV4 Hybrid.

2
00:00:04,600 --> 00:00:07,600
Her last contact
was seven days ago.

3
00:00:07,800 --> 00:00:10,200
Six days ago, that car sold.

4
00:00:10,400 --> 00:00:14,800
Meanwhile, a silver one sat
on the same lot for 74 days.

5
00:00:15,300 --> 00:00:18,300
Now multiply that by 24 stores.

6
00:00:18,500 --> 00:00:22,800
Every morning, over a thousand leads
like Maria are slipping away.

7
00:00:23,300 --> 00:00:26,500
Dealers don't lose these sales
for lack of cars.

8
00:00:26,700 --> 00:00:30,800
They lose them because nobody connects
the lead to the car in time.

9
00:00:31,050 --> 00:00:34,850
SalesDesk makes sure you never lose a sale
to a missed follow-up again.

10
00:00:35,100 --> 00:00:37,800
SalesDesk. Your AI sales analyst.

11
00:00:38,300 --> 00:00:41,800
At 2 AM, SalesDesk
starts its review.

12
00:00:41,800 --> 00:00:45,800
It splits the group into 24 jobs,
one per store,

13
00:00:45,800 --> 00:00:49,800
running in parallel
in isolated sandboxes on Vultr.

14
00:00:53,300 --> 00:00:56,300
Let's follow one store: Sandy.

15
00:00:56,300 --> 00:01:00,300
First, the agent reads every open lead
and flags the ones going cold:

16
00:01:00,300 --> 00:01:04,600
no contact in three days,
or the car they wanted is gone.

17
00:01:05,300 --> 00:01:09,800
Next, it searches every car on this lot
and at nearby sister stores,

18
00:01:09,800 --> 00:01:14,800
and scores each one against the request:
model, trim, budget, mileage.

19
00:01:14,800 --> 00:01:19,600
Cars that have sat the longest
get priority.

20
00:01:20,300 --> 00:01:25,300
Then Qwen, on Vultr Serverless Inference,
writes the store's morning brief

21
00:01:25,300 --> 00:01:30,600
and three personal follow-ups,
using only recorded vehicle facts.

22
00:01:31,300 --> 00:01:34,600
Two minutes, seven seconds later,
all 24 stores are done.

23
00:01:35,300 --> 00:01:37,800
Remember Maria?

24
00:01:37,800 --> 00:01:41,800
Here's what the agent found:
the silver RAV4 Hybrid on her own lot,

25
00:01:41,800 --> 00:01:44,800
a 98 out of 100 match.

26
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:48,800
It knows about her CR-V trade-in.
Her message is already written.

27
00:02:01,300 --> 00:02:06,300
At 7 AM, Sandy's manager opens
a ranked queue of 40 follow-ups

28
00:02:06,300 --> 00:02:09,800
and approves them in one click.

29
00:02:09,800 --> 00:02:12,800
Each salesperson gets
their tasks and drafts.

30
00:02:13,300 --> 00:02:18,800
Across the group, that's over a thousand
customers matched to a car in stock,

31
00:02:18,800 --> 00:02:24,600
and an estimated $3.4 million
in gross back in play.

32
00:02:25,300 --> 00:02:30,300
It all runs on Vultr: the scheduler
and sandboxes on a Vultr VM,

33
00:02:30,300 --> 00:02:36,600
and Qwen on Vultr Serverless Inference,
with validated drafts for manager review.

34
00:02:37,300 --> 00:02:41,200
SalesDesk. Every lead, every store,
every morning.

35
00:02:41,400 --> 00:02:44,600
Never lose a sale again.
